{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "simulation.py test cases (req D3 / build order 58)",
    "validates": "run_simulation(SimRequest) -> list[dict]. Covers presets, custom bands, flag tie-breaking, empty scenarios, and error paths.",
    "nature": "UNIT. All 'expect' values captured directly from running the real generate_arrivals/order_queue/run_simulation functions \u2014 not hand-computed.",
    "conventions": [
      "sim_id is assigned in ARRIVAL-TIME order (earliest arrival_epoch -> SIM-001), mirroring the real queue where a lower id means an earlier arrival; deterministic given the fixed seed.",
      "Sort key: the production SortKey (esi_band, flag_tier, arrival_epoch, intake_id) - lower esi_band first, then lower flag_tier (1=time-critical before 2=occult before 3=none), then earlier arrival_epoch; intake_id (int of sim_id) is the final tie-break.",
      "arrival_epoch = BASE_EPOCH (2026-06-26 18:56:57 UTC) + a seeded random offset in [0, 3600]s, so times/ordering are deterministic; the frontend shows time-only.",
      "flag_tier is null in output when no flag (matches PatientDetailOut's exclude_none convention elsewhere in the app).",
      "Empty counts (all n=0) return an empty list - this is NOT an error condition.",
      "Unknown preset name or a request with neither preset nor custom_bands both raise ValueError.",
      "This never touches the DB or the real queue - in-memory only, per the design decision."
    ]
  },
